{"name":"Light Thought","hex":"#e2d8d4","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"light","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye (about 400–750 nanometers): visible light.","Electromagnetic radiation in the wavelength range visible to the human eye or in nearby ranges (infrared or ultraviolet radiation)."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To start (a fire).","To set fire to; to set burning."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/light"},{"term":"thought","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A representation created in the mind without the use of one's faculties of vision, sound, smell, touch, or taste; an instance of thinking.","The operation by which mental activity arise or are manipulated; the process of thinking; the agency by which thinking is accomplished."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of think"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/thought"}],"entries":[{"title":"Thought","blocks":[{"text":"Thought, or thinking, is a cognitive process in which the mind considers, creates, or manipulates ideas, representations, or information. Core forms include judging, reasoning, concept formation, problem solving, and deliberation. Other processes, such as entertaining an idea, memory, or imagination, are also frequently considered types of thought. Thought may arise in response to perception, but can also occur without immediate input from the sensory organs. In a broader sense, any mental event—including perception and unconscious processes—may be described as forms of thought. The term can also denote not the process itself, but the resulting mental states or systems of ideas."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/53/Jardin_du_Musee_Rodin_Paris_Le_Penseur_20050402_%2802%29.jpg/330px-Jardin_du_Musee_Rodin_Paris_Le_Penseur_20050402_%2802%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thought","wikidata":"Q9420"},{"title":"Light","blocks":[{"text":"Light, visible light, or visible radiation is electromagnetic radiation that can be perceived by the human eye. Visible light spans the visible spectrum and is usually defined as having wavelengths in the range of 400–700 nanometers (nm), corresponding to frequencies of 750–420 terahertz. The visible band sits adjacent to the infrared and the ultraviolet, called collectively optical radiation."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fa/Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg/330px-Prism_flat_rainbow_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Light","wikidata":"Q9128"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Thinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg/500px-Thinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/23/Thinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg/500px-Thinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Man thinking on a train journey","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThinking%E0%A7%A8.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/500px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/1280px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_Sicilia.JPG/500px-Rocca_dell%27Abisso%2C_Fondachelli_Fantina%2C_S